From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: account TX before ring publication

Once the TCL producer pointer is published, another CPU can process
its completion and release the skb. Increment the pending count before
publication, so a concurrent completion cannot decrement an unaccounted
packet and miss the wakeup of a flush waiter.

The debug dump also dereferences the skb after publication. Move it
before the DMA mapping, while the buffer is still CPU-owned; label it as
an attempted TX because subsequent submission can fail.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
@@ -257,6 +257,8 @@
 		hdr = (void *)skb->data;
 	}
 map:
+	ath12k_dbg_dump(ab, ATH12K_DBG_DP_TX, NULL, "dp tx msdu attempt: ",
+			skb->data, skb->len);
 	ti.paddr = dma_map_single(dp->dev, skb->data, skb->len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
 	if (dma_mapping_error(dp->dev, ti.paddr)) {
 		atomic_inc(&dp->device_stats.tx_err.misc_fail);
@@ -375,15 +377,12 @@
 
 	ath12k_wifi7_hal_tx_cmd_desc_setup(ab, hal_tcl_desc, &ti);
 
+	/* Completions can run on another CPU as soon as the ring is published. */
+	atomic_inc(&dp_pdev->num_tx_pending);
 	ath12k_hal_srng_access_end(ab, tcl_ring);
 
 	spin_unlock_bh(&tcl_ring->lock);
 
-	ath12k_dbg_dump(ab, ATH12K_DBG_DP_TX, NULL, "dp tx msdu: ",
-			skb->data, skb->len);
-
-	atomic_inc(&dp_pdev->num_tx_pending);
-
 	return 0;
 
 fail_unmap_dma_ext:
